# Memory Bank — Always On

The Memory Bank is stored at `docs/memory-bank/` (local only; not committed). It consists of three files: `systemPatterns.md`, `techContext.md`, `progress.md`.

## What to read

Before answering any question or generating any code in this repository:

1. Read and internalize `docs/memory-bank/systemPatterns.md` — engineering contract for the repo. Comply with the patterns defined there.
2. If a request conflicts with `systemPatterns.md`, do not silently comply. Explain the conflict and propose a compliant alternative.
3. When generating a new file or component, verify the correct location using `docs/memory-bank/techContext.md` when it exists. 
4. Read `docs/memory-bank/progress.md` to understand current active tasks, recently completed features, and any recent blockers.

If a given file is missing, treat it as empty context. You are allowed to create `systemPatterns.md` or `techContext.md` if you need to save an architectural insight or document new context.